sequenceDiagram
    participant USER as User process<br/>(target binary)
    participant K as Kernel<br/>uprobes
    participant BPF as BPF<br/>program
    participant LD as libbpf<br/>at attach

    Note over USER,LD: One-time attach
    LD->>K: open /usr/bin/bash<br/>find symbol readline<br/>at offset 0x4f200
    LD->>K: register uprobe<br/>at inode+offset
    K->>K: insert breakpoint (int3)<br/>at first instruction<br/>via /proc/self/mem-style write
    Note over K: All processes loading<br/>/usr/bin/bash get the<br/>breakpoint (via copy-on-<br/>write on first execute)

    Note over USER,BPF: Runtime — every readline() call
    USER->>USER: bash calls<br/>readline(prompt)
    USER->>USER: int3 trap fires!
    USER->>K: kernel handles trap
    K->>BPF: invoke uprobe BPF<br/>program with pt_regs
    BPF->>BPF: read prompt from RDI<br/>via bpf_probe_read_user_str
    BPF-->>K: return
    K->>K: emulate the<br/>original instruction
    K-->>USER: resume readline()
